Chapter: EffectWidenScopeNarrow
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16

Section: Body

 A scope inside another scope is safe to hand over, and working out
 whether it IS inside needs to know what the scope means.

 `deep-read` reads only under "/config/app/". A parameter declared over
 "/config/" promises its caller no more than reads under "/config/", and
 "/config/app/" is under "/config/", so the argument does less than the
 parameter promised. The argument boundary refused this until the relation
 existed.

 The relation is chosen by the effect's family, off its own name, exactly
 as `scope-admits` has always chosen it: a filesystem scope is a path
 prefix, a network scope an authority, a console scope a channel. It is
 `scope-subsumes`, and it is deliberately NOT `scope-admits` -- see
 errors/effect-widen-scope-port for the one clause that separates them and
 the laundering it would have caused.

 The unsound direction ships beside this as errors/effect-widen-scope-out:
 a "/config/" argument does NOT pass where "/config/app/" is expected,
 because it may read things the parameter promised it would not.

  deep-read : Text -> [FileSystem.Read "/config/app/", Device.Block] Boolean
  deep-read (p) = file-exists "/config/app/settings.txt"

  apply-cfg : (Text -> [FileSystem.Read "/config/", Device.Block] Boolean), Text -> [FileSystem.Read "/config/", Device.Block] Boolean
  apply-cfg (f) (p) = f p

  opening : [Console, FileSystem.Read "/config/", Device.Block] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (if apply-cfg deep-read "/config/app/settings.txt" then "found" else "narrowed")
  end
